IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qld-part10-service-of-documents`

-- Tests for Part 10 (qld-part10-service-of-documents.l4).
-- Each expected value was worked out by hand from the text, as cited.
-- The time service by post is taken to have been effected (s 39A(1)(b)) is tested in qld-tests-time.l4.

§ `Tests of Part 10`

-- SAYS A document may be served on an individual by delivering it personally, by leaving it at, or by sending it by post, telex, facsimile or similar facility to, the last known address of residence or business (s 39(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` TRUE `an individual` `by delivering it to the person personally` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` TRUE `an individual` `by leaving it at the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` TRUE `an individual` `by sending it by post, telex, facsimile or similar facility to the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` TRUE `an individual` `by leaving it at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` TRUE `an individual` `in any other way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` TRUE `a body corporate` `by leaving it at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` TRUE `a body corporate` `by sending it by post, telex, facsimile or similar facility to the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` TRUE `a body corporate` `by delivering it to the person personally` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` FALSE `an individual` `by delivering it to the person personally` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsection (1) applies whichever expression is used (s 39(2))` deliver EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsection (1) applies whichever expression is used (s 39(2))` give EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsection (1) applies whichever expression is used (s 39(2))` notify EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsection (1) applies whichever expression is used (s 39(2))` send EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsection (1) applies whichever expression is used (s 39(2))` serve EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsection (1) applies whichever expression is used (s 39(2))` `another expression` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39(1) affects the operation of another law that authorises the service of a document otherwise than as provided in the subsection (s 39(3)(a))` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 39(1) affects the power of a court or tribunal to authorise service of a document otherwise than as provided in the subsection (s 39(3)(b))` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `service by post may be effected (s 39A(1)(a))` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `service by post may be effected (s 39A(1)(a))` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `service by post may be effected (s 39A(1)(a))` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the requirement or permission to serve by a particular postal method is taken to be satisfied (s 39A(2))` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirement or permission to serve by a particular postal method is taken to be satisfied (s 39A(2))` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirement or permission to serve by a particular postal method is taken to be satisfied (s 39A(2))` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the requirement or permission to serve by a particular postal method is taken to be satisfied (s 39A(2))` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsections (1) and (2) apply whichever expression is used (s 39A(3))` serve EQUALS JUST TRUE
